1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:02,090
Hello, fellow aliens.

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:06,860
Today we will learn about seemingly simple
words like "Hello", "Please", or "Thank you",

3
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:09,530
and about the complex interactions behind
them.

4
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:48,690
We may call these interactions "Social mechanics".

5
00:00:48,690 --> 00:00:52,369
Galactic protocols require that the first
sentence of any first contact must be the

6
00:00:52,369 --> 00:00:54,210
sentence "We come in peace".

7
00:00:54,210 --> 00:00:55,699
This is called a greeting.

8
00:00:55,699 --> 00:01:02,489
Of course, this sentence is optional in case
you don't actually come in peace.

9
00:01:02,489 --> 00:01:05,159
Earthlings always greet each other when they
encounter.

10
00:01:05,159 --> 00:01:08,009
They are not the only race to do so.

11
00:01:08,009 --> 00:01:11,710
The Lava Golems from Sanguis 4 for example
greet each other by describing what they will

12
00:01:11,710 --> 00:01:14,689
do if ever they meet in mortal combat.

13
00:01:14,689 --> 00:01:18,920
One Golem may say: "I will rip your guts out
and wrap them around your head!", to which

14
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:23,979
the other one may reply "I will turn you inside
out and cover you with yellow sauce!"

15
00:01:23,979 --> 00:01:27,750
And that's only how they greet the mailman
- greetings between close siblings or written

16
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:29,659
greetings are much longer.

17
00:01:29,659 --> 00:01:33,200
For Golems, greeting serve to show off social
dominance.

18
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,000
Earthling greetings have another purpose.

19
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,030
It has to do with so-called social relationships.

20
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:41,520
To understand this, let me disgress a bit.

21
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:42,840
This is a sofa.

22
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,710
Its' purpose doesn't matter here.

23
00:01:44,710 --> 00:01:45,710
What matters is that

24
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:47,729
A) Many earthlings have a sofa,

25
00:01:47,729 --> 00:01:51,859
B) Earthlings take their sofa with them when
they move, and, most importantly,

26
00:01:51,859 --> 00:01:55,320
C) You need more than one earthling to move
a sofa.

27
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:59,909
So, earthlings need to cooperate to move all
those sofas around, which makes them perfect

28
00:01:59,909 --> 00:02:06,560
examples for how earthlings organize cooperation.

29
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:10,110
The key to cooperation management is social
relationships.

30
00:02:10,110 --> 00:02:15,280
Besides family bonds, earthlings create more
or less intense bonds with other earthlings.

31
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:20,110
The intensity of the relationship determines
the level of cooperation.

32
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:22,989
For example, a stranger would not care about
your sofa.

33
00:02:22,989 --> 00:02:25,990
An acquaintance would sit on your sofa when
you invite him.

34
00:02:25,990 --> 00:02:28,170
A friend would help you moving your sofa,

35
00:02:28,170 --> 00:02:31,290
and a lover would want to have sex with you
on the sofa.

36
00:02:31,290 --> 00:02:36,250
Now, as the intensity of relationships changes
over time, earthlings need to synchronize

37
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:38,340
the perceived relationship level.

38
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:39,810
That's where greetings come in.

39
00:02:39,810 --> 00:02:42,299
Each level has its own greeting rituals.

40
00:02:42,299 --> 00:02:44,630
Acquaintantes use formal greetings,

41
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:46,390
friends more informal greetings,

42
00:02:46,390 --> 00:02:50,269
and lovers get all touchy and kissy and give
each other cute animal names.

43
00:02:50,269 --> 00:02:55,280
Also, greetings serve to communicate and synchronize
other information, like differences in social

44
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:56,380
status.

45
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:59,700
Tips for tourists:

46
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:03,819
When you make first contact, you can use the
formula "I come in peace".

47
00:03:03,819 --> 00:03:06,959
Anyway, earthlings will expect you to say
something outlandish.

48
00:03:06,959 --> 00:03:12,360
However, the formula "Bring me to your leader"
won't be very helpful, as most earthlings'

49
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:15,640
social rank is to low to know their country's
leader personally.

50
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:19,569
The best you can expect is a meeting with
some local official.

51
00:03:19,569 --> 00:03:23,880
To understand words like "Please" or "Thank
you", we need to understand another mechanism:

52
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:24,880
Gratitude.

53
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:29,180
When trading goods or services with strangers,
Earthlings use money - a virtual trade good

54
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:31,299
I will explain in another episode.

55
00:03:31,299 --> 00:03:35,470
But for trade with friends and family they
use mostly another virtual currency called

56
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:39,940
gratitude, which is - unlike money - always
bound to one relationship.

57
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:43,660
Take, for example, an earthling A who needs
help to move his sofa.

58
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:48,049
He approaches B who greets him with "Hello,
my friend", which indicates to A that they

59
00:03:48,049 --> 00:03:49,510
are still friends.

60
00:03:49,510 --> 00:03:54,640
So, A can offer B an exchange: Gratitude against
help with the sofa.

61
00:03:54,640 --> 00:04:00,150
To initiate the exchange, A uses the ritual
word "Please", which indicates a trade offer:

62
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:01,670
Favour against gratitude.

63
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:06,170
If B isn't interested in the trade, A may
even increase the amount of offered gratitude,

64
00:04:06,170 --> 00:04:09,760
by changing the formula to something like
"Pretty please" or "please please please with

65
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:11,079
a cherry on top".

66
00:04:11,079 --> 00:04:15,290
It's basically a kind of bargaining, except
that the currency is gratitude.

67
00:04:15,290 --> 00:04:19,440
Now, let's say B accepts the trade offer and
helps him with his sofa.

68
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:22,890
As agreed upon, A gives B gratitude in exchange.

69
00:04:22,890 --> 00:04:25,500
He does so with the ritual formula "Thank
you".

70
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:29,090
B receives the gratitude with another ritual
formula, "You're welcome".

71
00:04:29,090 --> 00:04:33,320
The exact formulae may vary, in order to indicate
the amount of gratitude.

72
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:37,850
This is very important, to keep the perceived
gratitude scores synchronized.

73
00:04:37,850 --> 00:04:41,420
B can then use the gratitude whenever he wants
a favour from A.

74
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:46,030
If A wants some gratitude back but B doesn't
make a trade offer, he can do him a favour,

75
00:04:46,030 --> 00:04:49,030
or he can give him an object in exchange for
gratitude.

76
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:50,580
This is called a gift.

77
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:55,010
Friends often exchange gifts, this improves
the friendship and allows balancing the gratitude

78
00:04:55,010 --> 00:04:56,010
level.

79
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:59,440
The strange thing about gratitude is that
it is not exactly quantifiable or measurable

80
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:03,360
- most earthlings don't even realize that
it's a virtual trade good.

81
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:07,870
But maintaining the gratitude flow is crucial
for the functioning of any personal relationship.

82
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:13,780
Actually, a relationship where one part gives
and gives without receiving is called "exploitation".

83
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:17,280
Or sometimes "friend zone".

84
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:19,780
Scientific advice:

85
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:23,160
If you have a time machine, you can make the
following experiment: Abduct an earthling,

86
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:26,390
bring him back in time and make him meet himself.

87
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:31,650
The goal is to create a conflict situation
- say, finding some delicious food after several

88
00:05:31,650 --> 00:05:33,310
days without eating.

89
00:05:33,310 --> 00:05:36,900
Many earthlings will come to the conclusion
that social rules don't apply to their own

90
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:45,870
time clones, which can lead to very interesting
situations.

91
00:05:45,870 --> 00:05:56,860
Now, what happens if B does something bad
to A, like ruining his sofa by accident?

92
00:05:56,860 --> 00:06:01,300
There is another mechanism for this kind of
situation: In this case, B is considered at

93
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,590
fault, which has three consequences:

94
00:06:03,590 --> 00:06:08,200
First, B is punished by the feeling of guilt,
caused by his own niggler in his head.

95
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:13,260
Second, A resents B for a while, which is
just a ritual to communicate fault and maintain

96
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:14,260
guilt.

97
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:19,300
Third, to end this situation, B has to use
another ritual formula, "Please excuse me"

98
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:20,300
or "Sorry".

99
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:25,201
As we have learned before, the word "please"
opens a gratitude trade - in this case, gratitude

100
00:06:25,201 --> 00:06:26,950
against purging the fault.

101
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:32,150
If A accepts the trade, he gets the gratitude
and stops resenting B, and everything is as

102
00:06:32,150 --> 00:06:37,940
before - except for the ruined sofa and the
modified gratitude scores.

103
00:06:37,940 --> 00:06:39,390
Strategic advice:

104
00:06:39,390 --> 00:06:42,270
"Sorry" is a very powerful word.

105
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:46,360
When you attack earth, you might destroy one
big earthling city, and then transmit the

106
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:47,890
message "We are so sorry."

107
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:52,170
If you banter something about technical issues
or cultural misunderstandings, odds are that

108
00:06:52,170 --> 00:06:53,980
earthlings will believe you.

109
00:06:53,980 --> 00:07:00,790
However, this trick won't work a second time.

110
00:07:00,790 --> 00:07:09,520
Greetings, thanks and excuses are rituals
- symbolic actions which don't actually do

111
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:12,610
anything, but have an important place in earthling
society.

112
00:07:12,610 --> 00:07:15,220
We will talk about rituals in another episode.

113
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:19,520
By the way, ritualistic behaviour is common
amongst mobile lifeforms on earth.

114
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:24,280
Except for the microbes.

115
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:27,640
Not everything can be explained with gratitude
points, though.

116
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:32,160
In large earthling settlements, you often
see individuals called beggars who ask complete

117
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:35,740
strangers for money, using the ritual word
"please".

118
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:40,310
Some alien scienists describe those beggars
as "gratitude traders", but that doesn't make

119
00:07:40,310 --> 00:07:41,310
sense:

120
00:07:41,310 --> 00:07:44,030
Why should an earthling buy the gratitude
of a stranger who will never ever help him

121
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:45,330
with his sofa?

122
00:07:45,330 --> 00:07:49,160
And why should someone accumulate gratitude
debts he can never expect to be able to pay

123
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:50,160
back?

124
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:53,900
I think there is another social mechanism
behind this: Karma.

125
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:57,090
Most earthlings have the more or less vague
feeling that there is some kind of invisible

126
00:07:57,090 --> 00:08:01,500
point system, that you get points by being
good and lose points by being bad.

127
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:04,000
Some earthlings call these points "Karma".

128
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,620
Some believe that karma is rewarded in the
afterlife, in the next reincarnation, in this

129
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:10,390
life, or not at all.

130
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:14,620
But anyway, getting Karma causes a pleasant
feeling of superiority, and makes the niggler

131
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:17,080
in the head shut up for a while.

132
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:22,120
If you consider Karma as a virtual exchange
good, like money or gratitude, things become

133
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:26,740
a lot clearer: Beggars are actual karma producers
who sell their product on the street.

134
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:30,710
Karma becomes kind of a luxury good: It's
not vital, but it makes you feel good and

135
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:32,740
helps to display your wealth.

136
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:35,959
Not everybody buys karma directly from the
producer, though.

137
00:08:35,959 --> 00:08:40,219
Many cities have intermediaries like soup
kitchen where karma producers - poor earthlings

138
00:08:40,219 --> 00:08:45,540
- can sell their karma against food, and rich
earthlings can buy karma against money.

139
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:48,550
And that's not all: Karma is big business!

140
00:08:48,550 --> 00:08:52,389
Whenever earthlings in a region are struck
by a natural catastrophe, international karma

141
00:08:52,389 --> 00:08:57,209
traders show up within hours, provide help,
harvest karma and sell it to people in rich

142
00:08:57,209 --> 00:08:58,670
countries.

143
00:08:58,670 --> 00:09:03,209
This is called "humanitarian aid", but it
is nothing else than world-wide karma trade.

144
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:07,640
Roughly speaking, poor countries are in general
karma exporters, whereas rich countries are

145
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:09,310
generally karma importers.

146
00:09:09,310 --> 00:09:13,250
Karma comes, so to say, in different flavours.

147
00:09:13,250 --> 00:09:16,420
Besides humanitarian karma there exist, for
example,

148
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:17,759
animal protection karma,

149
00:09:17,759 --> 00:09:18,959
ecology karma,

150
00:09:18,959 --> 00:09:19,959
religious karma,

151
00:09:19,959 --> 00:09:21,019
patriotic karma,

152
00:09:21,019 --> 00:09:22,339
pacifist karma,

153
00:09:22,339 --> 00:09:24,490
and karma for buying from a specific company.

154
00:09:24,490 --> 00:09:29,139
A personal word to my earthling viewers: If
you want some alien-flavoured karma, click

155
00:09:29,139 --> 00:09:31,959
on Like, subscribe and tell all your friends.

156
00:09:31,959 --> 00:09:36,079
And if you draw the attention of a popular
blogger, Youtuber, rockstar, or whoever might

157
00:09:36,079 --> 00:09:40,170
bring me new traffic, I may also throw in
some personal gratitude.

158
00:09:40,170 --> 00:09:44,470
In case you wonder why you would want the
gratitude of a 3 feet high alien, I only say

159
00:09:44,470 --> 00:09:46,970
one word:

160
00:09:46,970 --> 00:09:48,930
Teleportation!

161
00:09:48,930 --> 00:09:53,829
In the next episode, I will explain something
that most aliens find very puzzling: Funny

162
00:09:53,829 --> 00:09:58,960
things, humour, and the strange noises earthlings
make when they find something funny.

163
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:19,489
Thanks for watching, and don't forget to be
alien!

